{
    "word": "tchotchke",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "09a1ca81-b733-31e1-8ce8-1a3a36cd8a09",
                "word": "tchotchke",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "98995fe8-993c-4f45-8c9f-a14a061f5a67",
                        "entry_id": "09a1ca81-b733-31e1-8ce8-1a3a36cd8a09",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "tchotchkes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d238bc8d-5f50-3f96-8f7e-86029504cbb1",
                        "entry_id": "09a1ca81-b733-31e1-8ce8-1a3a36cd8a09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small ornament of minor value; a knick-knack, a trinket."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56ee5f21-c986-4417-8065-1d575a24948f",
                                "sense_id": "d238bc8d-5f50-3f96-8f7e-86029504cbb1",
                                "text": "We're stuck with: 14 Provincial & Modern Kitchen chairs— […] 23 assorted Lamps and miscellaneous \"Tchotchkes\"! Help us unload."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "176bb9c2-28bb-44a5-897b-7fcb0e476dff",
                                "sense_id": "d238bc8d-5f50-3f96-8f7e-86029504cbb1",
                                "text": "Barbra Streisand's ambition: to open a knick-knack shop called \"Tchotchkes\" (Yiddish for \"knick-knacks\") …"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "076104ad-1733-4ce3-8d7a-8a1cae6ac281",
                                "sense_id": "d238bc8d-5f50-3f96-8f7e-86029504cbb1",
                                "text": "The idea of a discount operation, of course, is that it shouldn't look like a boutique. Presumably the price tags are decoration enough. \"Décor doesn't add to the glamour of a suit,\" an owner pointed out. \"You're not buying the rugs or the lamps or the tsatskes.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "102e9ca1-d948-4b7b-b2e7-63942c77cbc6",
                                "sense_id": "d238bc8d-5f50-3f96-8f7e-86029504cbb1",
                                "text": "I am a child of modernism – […] As such I have inherited a distrust of the tchotchke, which I have still – even as the house I was raised in of course had its share of (modernist) tchotchkes: the Asian art, the Danish designware, the Indian pottery, the MoMA catalogues."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26fc7570-5439-49cf-82b5-bcce8d826741",
                                "sense_id": "d238bc8d-5f50-3f96-8f7e-86029504cbb1",
                                "text": "With limited cash and a thirst for uncommon sights, backpackers have pushed into challenging territory well before the big-money resorts or tchotchke merchants."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "881464c9-c860-46ce-a3bb-c1e9ee4f9c31",
                                "sense_id": "d238bc8d-5f50-3f96-8f7e-86029504cbb1",
                                "text": "The awsome dissonance of Psycho works independently even as it instantly evokes Norman Bates's stabbing knife and Marion Crane's helpless scream. Once again [Alfred] Hitchcock overturned the convention that music must remain subliminally in the background of a film: […] in its quiet moments, it roams grimly wherever it pleases, investing the most banal images—a toy, a car on an empty highway, a suitcase on a bed, a tchotchke of folding hands—with dread."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e1455b4-9234-48ad-ab43-34a32ef1a5a7",
                                "sense_id": "d238bc8d-5f50-3f96-8f7e-86029504cbb1",
                                "text": "“The night market is a bit like the famous Italian street fairs of Little Italy. Very diverse. Lots of different cultures represented. Sticky shit all over the ground. And a good place to pillage or barter tchotchkes.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "71c2a459-faf5-3723-a43f-14f49ce453b5",
                        "entry_id": "09a1ca81-b733-31e1-8ce8-1a3a36cd8a09",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An attractive girl or woman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "dated",
                            "figuratively",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f78073e2-9e75-43e0-a1a3-599bd64d6d3b",
                                "sense_id": "71c2a459-faf5-3723-a43f-14f49ce453b5",
                                "text": "My mother is still convinced that her little boy doesn't eat enough (I've gained 15 pounds the last six months), and that he doesn't get enough sleep (I average a good nine hours a night), […] She is always giving me advice, chiding me for the error of my ways, warning me not to drive too fast, and in general behaving as if her tsatske hasn't got enough sense to get in out of the rain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "931244a9-983f-45f6-b5f8-612f503cc3d7",
                                "sense_id": "71c2a459-faf5-3723-a43f-14f49ce453b5",
                                "text": "He looked Elinor over appraisingly as she seated herself on the banquette between him and Jake. \"A real tsatskeh,\" he said with approval."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "38eb7008-54eb-42ca-aa52-786f289160c7",
                                "sense_id": "71c2a459-faf5-3723-a43f-14f49ce453b5",
                                "text": "The Business Section of the admirable New York Times once published advertisements that showed a full-bosomed tchotchke in a very skimpy bra and panties leaning forward invitingly. The caption under this photograph read: / hi—i'm evelyn / and I'm Available / for / Trade Shows / Conventions / Business Meetings"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
